@startuml 05_spinlock
title 5. Spinlock: waiting by spinning (Experiments 4-5)
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

start
:exchange(flag, true)\ntry to take the lock;
while (got it?) is (no: flag was already true)
  :spin: read flag in a loop\nwith _mm_pause();
  :exchange(flag, true)\nagain;
endwhile (yes)
:critical section\n++counter;
:store(flag, false)\nrelease the lock;
stop

footer Never sleeps, so it is cheap with one thread (about 1.5 ns per increment). With many threads every release invalidates every spinner's copy, and throughput collapses.
@enduml
